{{ for pair in _meta.frontMatter }}
{{ pair.key }}: {{ pair.value -}}
{{ end }}
exportedAt: {{ _meta.exportedAtUtc | date.to_string "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ" }}
environment: {{ _meta.environment.url }}

---

# Relationships — {{ _meta.environment.orgName }}

> Scope: the project's relationships — custom (created by a maker, not by the platform) and unmanaged. System relationships every table gets (owner, created by, notes, activities and so on) and relationships installed by managed solutions are left out, as is a managed relationship whose behavior the project changed.

{{
  table_names = {}
  for t in tables
    table_names[t.LogicalName] = t.DisplayName | display_label t.LogicalName
  end

  func table_ref(name)
    $display = table_names[name]
    if $display == null || $display == name
      ret "`" + name + "`"
    end
    ret "`" + name + "` (" + $display + ")"
  end

  func cell(text)
    if text == null
      ret ""
    end
    ret ("" + text) | string.replace "|" "\\|" | string.replace "\r" "" | string.replace "\n" " "
  end

  cascade_labels = {}
  cascade_labels["Cascade"] = "Cascade all"
  cascade_labels["Active"] = "Cascade active"
  cascade_labels["UserOwned"] = "Cascade user-owned"
  cascade_labels["NoCascade"] = "None"
  cascade_labels["RemoveLink"] = "Remove link"
  cascade_labels["Restrict"] = "Restrict"

  # The behaviors offered when a relationship is configured, from Assign, Delete, Reparent, Share and Unshare.
  func behavior(c)
    if c == null
      ret "—"
    end
    $others = [c.Assign, c.Reparent, c.Share, c.Unshare]
    $all_cascade = c.Delete == "Cascade"
    $all_none = true
    for $v in $others
      if $v != "Cascade"; $all_cascade = false; end
      if $v != "NoCascade"; $all_none = false; end
    end
    if $all_cascade
      ret "Parental"
    end
    if $all_none && c.Delete == "RemoveLink"
      ret "Referential"
    end
    if $all_none && c.Delete == "Restrict"
      ret "Referential, restrict delete"
    end
    ret "Custom"
  end

  # Cascade settings grouped by value: "Delete: Remove link; Assign, Merge, …: None".
  func cascade(c)
    if c == null
      ret "—"
    end
    $by_value = {}
    $order = []
    for $action in ["Delete", "Assign", "Share", "Unshare", "Reparent", "Merge"]
      $v = c[$action]
      if $v == null
        continue
      end
      $label = cascade_labels[$v] ?? $v
      if $by_value[$label] == null
        $by_value[$label] = []
        $order = $order | array.add $label
      end
      $by_value[$label] = $by_value[$label] | array.add $action
    end
    $parts = []
    for $label in $order
      $parts = $parts | array.add (($by_value[$label] | array.join ", ") + ": " + $label)
    end
    ret $parts | array.join "; "
  end

  # Where the related records appear on the primary table's form navigation.
  func menu(m)
    if m == null
      ret "—"
    end
    if m.Behavior == "DoNotDisplay"
      ret "Hidden"
    end
    $text = m.Behavior == "UseLabel" ? (m.Label | display_label "(label)") : "Collection name"
    ret m.Group != null ? ($text + " (" + m.Group + ")") : $text
  end

  one_to_many = oneToMany | array.sort "SchemaName"
  many_to_many = manyToMany | array.sort "SchemaName"
  referenced_tables = one_to_many | pluck "ReferencedEntity" | array.sort
  referencing_tables = one_to_many | pluck "ReferencingEntity" | array.sort
-}}
| One-to-many | Many-to-many | Primary tables | Tables with project lookups |
|---|---|---|---|
| {{ one_to_many.size }} | {{ many_to_many.size }} | {{ referenced_tables.size }} | {{ referencing_tables.size }} |

**Reading the tables.** A one-to-many relationship adds a lookup column to the related (many) table that points to the primary (one) table. **Behavior** is the relationship type as configured: *Parental* cascades every action from the primary record to its related records, *Referential* removes the link when the primary record is deleted, *Referential, restrict delete* blocks the delete while related records exist, *Custom* is any other combination, detailed in **Cascade**. **Navigation** gives the Web API navigation properties: the single-valued one on the related table (set the lookup with `<name>@odata.bind`) and the collection on the primary table (`$expand=<name>`). **Related menu** is how the related records appear on the primary table's form.

## One-to-many relationships

Grouped by primary table.
{{ for group in one_to_many | group_by_key "ReferencedEntity" | array.sort "key" }}
### {{ table_ref group.key }}

| Related table | Lookup column | Schema name | Behavior | Cascade | Navigation (lookup / collection) | Related menu |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
{{ for r in group.items | array.sort "ReferencingEntity" -}}
| {{ table_ref r.ReferencingEntity }} | `{{ r.ReferencingAttribute }}` | `{{ r.SchemaName }}` | {{ behavior r.CascadeConfiguration }}{{ if r.IsHierarchical }} (hierarchical){{ end }} | {{ cascade r.CascadeConfiguration }} | `{{ r.ReferencingEntityNavigationPropertyName ?? "—" }}` / `{{ r.ReferencedEntityNavigationPropertyName ?? "—" }}` | {{ cell (menu r.AssociatedMenuConfiguration) }} |
{{ end -}}
{{ end }}
{{- if one_to_many.size == 0 }}
_No project one-to-many relationships._
{{ end }}
## Many-to-many relationships

Each is stored in an intersect table with one lookup to each side. **Navigation** gives the collection-valued navigation property on each table, used to associate records (`POST …/<name>/$ref`) and to `$expand`.

{{ if many_to_many.size > 0 -}}
| Schema name | Table 1 | Table 2 | Intersect table | Navigation (1 / 2) | Related menu (1 / 2) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
{{ for r in many_to_many -}}
| `{{ r.SchemaName }}` | {{ table_ref r.Entity1LogicalName }} | {{ table_ref r.Entity2LogicalName }} | `{{ r.IntersectEntityName }}` | `{{ r.Entity1NavigationPropertyName ?? "—" }}` / `{{ r.Entity2NavigationPropertyName ?? "—" }}` | {{ cell (menu r.Entity1AssociatedMenuConfiguration) }} / {{ cell (menu r.Entity2AssociatedMenuConfiguration) }} |
{{ end -}}
{{ else -}}
_No project many-to-many relationships._
{{ end }}
## Lookups by table

The project's lookup columns on each table and the tables they point to; a lookup that points to more than one table (a customer lookup, for example) lists each.

{{ for group in one_to_many | group_by_key "ReferencingEntity" | array.sort "key" -}}
{{-
  targets = {}
  columns = []
  for r in group.items
    if targets[r.ReferencingAttribute] == null
      targets[r.ReferencingAttribute] = []
      columns = columns | array.add r.ReferencingAttribute
    end
    targets[r.ReferencingAttribute] = targets[r.ReferencingAttribute] | array.add ("`" + r.ReferencedEntity + "`")
  end
  parts = []
  for col in columns | array.sort
    parts = parts | array.add ("`" + col + "` → " + (targets[col] | array.sort | array.join ", "))
  end
-}}
- {{ table_ref group.key }}: {{ parts | array.join " · " }}
{{ end -}}
